Subject: [PATCH] Fix Tab key behavior always detected as user defined (#16529)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Description

Closes #16526

`FeaturesPageView::refresh_tab_behavior_state` uppercased the displayed
keystroke before comparing it to `TAB_KEYSTROKE_STR` (`"Tab"`).
`Keystroke::displayed()` renders the Tab key as `"Tab"`, so the
comparison was effectively `"TAB" == "Tab"` and never matched; the Tab
key behavior always resolved to `TabBehavior::UserDefined`. As a result,
the hint line under the "Tab key behavior" dropdown disappeared right
after choosing an option, and the dropdown showed "User defined" once
the Features page was refreshed (e.g. after switching away and back).

This PR drops the two `.to_uppercase()` calls so the detection compares
the displayed keystroke directly, matching what
`set_tab_behavior_setting` in the same file already does. The
keybindings themselves were always applied correctly; only the detection
changes. No rendered strings change.

